{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/instructional-associate-continuing-track-department-of-biology-faculty-of-science-2/": {
      "title": "Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Bio… Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science The Department of Biology at Brandon University invites applications for the position of Instructional Associate with introductory emphasis in a continuing-track appointment to begin January 4, 2027, or as mutually agreed, subject to budgetary approval. The department of Biology is in a period of active growth and rejuvenation, particularly with respect to modernizing our undergraduate program. We seek an exceptional instructor with commitments to teaching excellence and pedagogical development, with that person able to adapt to a dynamic learning environment. The successful candidate will contribute to this momentum through a diverse repertoire of modern laboratory skills, and they will have outstanding skills in problem solving, communication, and organization. Responsibilities : The successful applicant will deliver in-person laboratories for up to five sections per week for 15:162 Cell, Genetics and Evolution (CGE) and 15:163 Biodiversity, Functions and Interactions (BFI), two team-taught first-year courses required by all Biology students at BU. As the CGE and BFI laboratory instructor, the successful applicant will be responsible for laboratory preparation, set-up, clean-up, laboratory safety, the preparation and marking of laboratory tests, the maintenance of laboratory records, coordination with other members of the CGE and BFI teaching teams regarding laboratory content and assessment, and the supervision of graduate students and undergraduate student assistants for marking, dishwashing, and the greenhouse. In cooperation with other departmental IAs, additional duties include ordering for laboratory classes for other Biology courses, ordering and receiving departmental supplies, maintaining and storing departmental equipment, and maintaining departmental teaching inventories. Qualifications : an M.Sc. in Biology or a related discipline is required, although a Ph.D. is preferred. Evidence of a successful record of laboratory instruction and demonstrated expertise in both traditional methods and molecular biological techniques is required. Applicants may seek to establish an experiential/traditional equivalency to the Master’s Degree and are invited to contact the Office of the Dean of Science on how to establish equivalent academic or professional credentials. Rank : Instructional Associate Salary : Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: October 6, 2026 or until position is filled. Start Date: January 4, 2027 Internal Applicants: Qualified internal applicants are invited to apply. Internal applicants are current full-time or part-time Brandon University Faculty Association (BUFA) Members on a continuing or regular appointment (does not include Contract Academic Staff (CAS)), CAS who hold RFR in one (1) or more courses in the Department of Biology, or the spouse/partner of a current full-time or part-time BUFA Member on a continuing or regular appointment. Internal applicants are required to identify as such in their letter of application. To Apply: Interested applicants are invited to submit an application package as one single electronic file (e.g., PDF) that must contain a letter of application (including details regarding area of specialization and experience relevant to the stated position requirements and preferences), a curriculum vitae, the names and contact information of three (3) references, statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages maximum), evidence of teaching effectiveness (course outlines, instructional material, teaching evaluations), and a statement on citizenship/Canadian immigration status to: Dr. Christophe LeMoine Dean of Science Brandon University Brandon, MB R7A 6A9 Science@BrandonU.ca We thank all applicants for their interest in applying for this position and advise that only candidates selected for interviews will be contacted. Short-listed candidates will be expected to provide copies of credentials at time of interview. Issued August 25, 2026 Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/2026-2027-winter-term-course-laboratory-based-contract-opportunities-department-of-applied-disaster-emergency-studies-ades-faculty-of-science/": {
      "title": "Top Toolbar Links",
      "description": "2026/2027, Winter Term, Course & Laboratory-Based Contract Opportunities, Department of Applied Disaster & Emergency Studies (ADES) – Faculty of Science | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities 2026/2027, Winter Term, Course & Laboratory-Based Contra… 2026/2027, Winter Term, Course & Laboratory-Based Contract Opportunities, Department of Applied Disaster & Emergency Studies (ADES) – Faculty of Science The Department of Applied Disaster and Emergency Studies (ADES) is seeking Contract Academic Staff to teach the course and/or lead the lab section for the course at Brandon University for the 2026 – 2027 academic year. Winter term: Classes run from January 5 to April 9, 2027, with an exam period following. Note: This job advertisement includes both a course and a laboratory section. Applicants may apply to either section: Course (3 credit hour) or Laboratory (1.5 credit hour) and qualified applicants may apply for both positions (4.5 credit hours total). 40.362 Disaster Response Management: Course and Laboratory Course: Section: A00 Tuesday Slot 13 1:40 pm – 4:30 pm (3 credit hour course) Laboratory: Section: Z10 Thursday Slot 14 1:40 pm – 4:30 pm (1.5 credit hour laboratory) Course description: 40:362 Disaster Response Management This course focuses on the theory and practice of how organizations manage their responses to emergencies and disasters. The use of incident management systems, emergency operation centres and other response techniques are considered from conceptual and practical perspectives. Disaster warning systems, evacuation planning, emergency social services, and related topics are examined. The course includes lab work in which students apply a selection of tools and techniques to become familiar with the roles of community members, government and non-government organizations and the private sector through activities in the Emergency Operations Lab (EOL). 3 class hours per week, and 3 laboratory hours per week, one term. Course Lecture Applicants: The course covers the following three 4-week modules. Applicants must indicate which module(s) they are qualified to deliver for 1 credit hour each. Applicants may apply for any or all modules. Response Coordination: Incident Management Systems, EOC management, critical infrastructure, psycho-social supports (CISM) Emergency Social Services: Evacuation, sheltering and emergency accommodation, ESS, donation/volunteer management Communications: Warning systems, crisis communication, interagency relationships, After Action Reports Qualifications for the Course Lecturer: A Master’s degree in Disaster and Emergency Management or a related discipline is required. Applicants must demonstrate relevant expertise in emergency management. Prior teaching or training experience is considered an asset. A preference will be given to candidates willing to teach in person in Brandon. In your cover letter, please indicate the module(s) (above) you are qualified to teach. Applicants may seek to establish an experiential/traditional equivalency to the Master’s degree are invited to contact the Chair of the Selection Committee at the address below on how to establish equivalent academic or professional credentials. Qualifications for the Lab Instructor: A Bachelor’s degree in Disaster and Emergency Management or a related disciplines is required. Applicants must have relevant expertise in the emergency management profession. A preference will be given to candidates willing to teach in person in Brandon. Successful teaching or training experience is preferred. Applicants may seek to establish an experiential/traditional equivalency to the Bachelor’s degree and are invited to contact the Chair of the Selection Committee at the address below on how to establish equivalent academic or professional credentials. Salary: $8,132 per 3 credit hour course Start date: Winter Term begins January 5, 2027 Application deadline: by 4:30 pm, October 16, 2026 Applications must be submitted via e-mail as a single, reasonably sized PDF file. The application should include the following: a letter of application, citizenship or Canadian immigration status, curriculum vitae, copies of transcripts, the names and contact information of three references. In your cover letter, clearly specify which of the above-listed course module(s) or/and laboratory section the applicant is applying to teach. Please send the application to: Dr. Christophe LeMoine Dean of Science Brandon University Brandon, MB R7A 6A9 science@brandonu.ca We thank all applicants for their interest in applying for this position and advise that only candidates selected for interviews will be contacted. Courses will run based on sufficient enrollment and budgetary approval. Issued Sept. 2. 2026 Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
