      "description": "Student Assistant III – Department of Chemistry | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant III – Department of Chemistry Student Assistant III – Department of Chemistry Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on October 15, 2026 Classification : Student Assistant III Employee Group : PSAC Job Title : Marker Department : Chemistry Wage or Salary : $18.73/hr Number of Hours to Work : Average of 5 hours per week, total of 40 hours Start Date: October 16, 2026 Number of Positions available : 1 End Date of Employment: December 23, 2026 Course title and number (if applicable): 18.363 Introductory Biochemistry Date Issued: October 8, 2026 Key Duties: The Department of Chemistry seeks a marker for Chem 18.363-Introductory Biochemistry. The marker will be involved in marking course tests, assignments, and exams with the use of a marking key, and other relevant duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Having successfully completed the course (18.363-Intro Biochemistry/Biochem I) or equivalent is required. Preference will be given to applicants with previous Introductory Biochemistry marking experience. To Apply: Interested applicants should contact Dr. Charette (CharetteM@BrandonU.ca) directly, and submit a brief cover letter and C.V., along with a brief description of their biochemistry experience. Only successful candidates will be contacted. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given 